# Kioku — the environment, by name only.
#
# ⚠️ **The remote is public** (`03` §13.1). Every value below stays out of the
# repository, out of issue bodies and out of comments. This file names the
# variables and carries no values, ever. Copy it to `.env`, which is gitignored.
#
# `03` §13.1 splits these across two processes on purpose: **the app tier never
# holds the model provider key.** Generation happens only in the worker, so the
# process with an internet-facing surface has no ability to spend money, and the
# process that can spend money has no internet-facing surface. That is easy to
# undo later by adding one convenience endpoint, which is why it is written down.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Nuxt app — Vercel environment variables, per environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ⚠️ The **pooled** Neon string (`-pooler` in the hostname), used **verbatim as
# issued** — ADR 0027: no `options=endpoint%3D…` rewriting, no hand-edited TLS
# parameters. `03` §4.1.
DATABASE_URL=

# Better Auth (`08` §10). These arrive with #5; named here so the five variables
# of `08` §10 live in one place.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# Sets `baseURL`, from which `trustedOrigins` and `secure` both derive.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# ⚠️ One value, and the process refuses to start without it (`08` §4.3).
KIOKU_INVITED_EMAIL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Python worker — a gitignored `.env` on the laptop, not Vercel
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ⚠️ The worker takes the **direct** string, not the pooled one. The pooled
# endpoint does not support `LISTEN`, so a worker pointed at it does not run
# slowly — **it silently never wakes** (`03` §4.1, verification §9.2). The
# variable is named separately from `DATABASE_URL` so nobody reaches for the
# wrong endpoint, and `worker/db.py` refuses a `-pooler` hostname at startup
# rather than letting the quiet version of that failure happen.
#
# ⚠️ Arrived with #7. `NOTIFY` is the half that *does* work through the pooler
# (PgBouncer's own matrix — ADR 0043), which is how the app sends the wake-up.
KIOKU_WORKER_DATABASE_URL=

# ⚠️ The model provider key, and it lives **only** here — never on Vercel
# (`03` §13.1). Arrived with #9, and the worker **refuses to start without it**:
# a worker that could not spend would drain the queue, produce nothing, and
# settle every run `complete`, which `03` §11 reads to the reader as a success.
# `test/unit/no-provider-key-in-the-app.test.ts` is the other half — the app tier
# may not name this variable at all.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ⚠️ **Optional, and the walk is the point** (ADR 0018). The working default is
# `claude-sonnet-5`, with `claude-opus-5` run once as a ceiling probe and the
# walk going *downward* toward `gpt-5.6-luna` until measured *acceptance rate*
# degrades — **which model wins is a measurement, not a document**. Moving
# between them is this variable plus an entry in `worker/prices.py`; every
# `ingestion` and every `note_field_provenance` row records which one ran, so
# the comparison is `04` §12's eighth query rather than a new experiment.
# KIOKU_MODEL_ID=

# ⚠️ **Optional, `laptop` or `server`, and it goes on the numbers** (`03` §12,
# `04` §6.1). Early *time-to-first-review* figures are not comparable across
# ADR 0022's move to EC2 or Lightsail, so the run records which side it ran on
# rather than leaving that in a paragraph. A value that is neither is refused at
# startup — a typo silently becoming `laptop` would put server figures in the
# laptop's column, which is the one comparison `03` §12 says must not be made.
# KIOKU_WORKER_ENVIRONMENT=
